# Copy to project root as `pytest.ini` (install.sh does this for Python stacks
# when no pytest config already exists in pyproject.toml/pytest.ini/tox.ini —
# including one in a subdirectory, see below).
# Minimal, standalone — like ruff.toml, it does not edit your pyproject.toml.
#
# MONOREPO WARNING. pytest reads exactly ONE ini-file, and the one at rootdir
# wins. If your Python project lives in a subdirectory (backend/, api/,
# services/x/) with its own [tool.pytest.ini_options], a pytest.ini at the repo
# ROOT silently overrides it — you lose settings like asyncio_mode, and the
# suite is only correct when invoked from that subdirectory. install.sh now
# detects that case and declines to write this file (#76); if you are copying it
# by hand, put it next to the Python project, not at the repo root.
#
# A runner forces nothing on its own. The opt-in patch-coverage gate
# (`.github/workflows/coverage.yml`, `install.sh --coverage-gate`) is what
# fails the build when CHANGED lines ship untested. See RECOMMENDATIONS.md.
[pytest]
# If ./tests does not exist, pytest treats testpaths as unmatched and collects
# from rootdir instead — so this line reads as "scoped" while behaving as
# "whole tree". Point it at your real test directory.
testpaths = tests
python_files = test_*.py *_test.py
# Defence in depth for the whole-tree fallback above, and for an explicit
# `pytest <path>` that reaches past testpaths. Anything on disk but not in git —
# a vendored toolchain, an agent worktree, an extra checkout — is otherwise
# inside collection's blast radius, and a vendored package's own tests fail on
# import with errors that have nothing to do with your code (#76).
#
# Setting this REPLACES pytest's default, so the default list is repeated here
# verbatim; only `.venv .tox .nox vendor third_party` are additions. The leading
# `.*` is what covers agent worktrees under `.claude/`.
#
# Deliberately conservative. pytest has NO .gitignore awareness, so this list is
# hand-written — and a too-broad entry (`tools`, `env`) silently stops collecting
# real tests, which is a worse failure than collecting too many: one is loud at
# the moment it happens, the other is invisible forever. Add your own vendored
# directories by name; do not add generic ones on spec.
norecursedirs = *.egg .* _darcs build CVS dist node_modules venv {arch} .venv .tox .nox vendor third_party
# -ra prints a summary of skips/xfails so silently-skipped tests stay visible.
addopts = -ra
